  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Angles \\(APO\\) and \\(ABM\\) are both right angles, and the two triangles share angle \\(A.\\) Therefore triangles \\(APO\\) and \\(ABM\\) are similar. Corresponding sides give \\[ \\frac{AP}{AB}=\\frac{AO}{AM}. \\] Hence \\(AP\\cdot AM=AO\\cdot AB.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Because \\(AB\\) is a diameter, angle \\(AMB\\) is a right angle",
        "Compare right triangles \\(APO\\) and \\(ABM\\)"
